# ============================================================================
# SECTION 8: Language Files (Selective)
# ============================================================================
# Keep: mhm-rentiva.pot, mhm-rentiva-tr_TR.po, mhm-rentiva-tr_TR.mo
# Keep: mhm-rentiva-de_DE.po, mhm-rentiva-de_DE.mo (German)
# Keep: languages/*.l10n.php -- WP 6.5+ loads these at runtime, so they SHIP.
#   Do not re-add an ignore rule for them. It was here until 2026-09-06 and the
#   only reason tr_TR survived is that someone had force-added it (`git add -f`);
#   a second locale's .l10n.php would have been dropped silently, with no error
#   at build time and no missing-file gate to catch it. Pro's .gitignore never
#   had the rule -- the two trees had disagreed since WP 6.5.
languages/*-backup-*.pot~
languages/*-backup-*.po~
# React/JS i18n: WordPress core resolves a script handle's translations to
# `mhm-rentiva-<locale>-md5(<src relative to plugin root>).json`. The React
# admin scripts register src `build/admin/<page>.js`, so the ONLY files WP
# loads are `mhm-rentiva-<locale>-<md5>.json`. These md5-named files are the
# canonical runtime set and MUST be committed so a clean clone ships a
# translated React admin (regenerate deterministically via
# `python bin/build-i18n.py`). They are intentionally NOT ignored.
#
# The old handle-named `*-mhm-rentiva-react-*.json` files were vestigial —
# WP never loaded them (md5 resolution only) — and have been removed.
languages/mhm-rentiva-en_US.*
# `wp i18n make-json --use-map` input: maps every src-react source to the
# build/admin/<entry>.js bundle it compiles into. Deliberately NOT committed —
# bin/build-i18n.py regenerates it from webpack's entry list on every run, so
# it cannot drift the way a checked-in copy would.
.i18n-map.json

