!bin/BUILD.md
# The .pot recipe. Tracked because the project's "makepot scope must match the
# committed .pot" rule is unenforceable while the --exclude set lives only in
# somebody's shell history: there is no way to check what the committed catalog
# was built with. This file makes the scope a committed fact, and carries the
# probe command that proves a regeneration changed only real strings.
!bin/make-pot.sh
# Required by tests/Migration/MetaMigrationTest.php (it include()s this CLI
# script). Must be tracked or every clean clone fails 4 migration tests —
# the recurrence the unmerged 362a475 "restore missing scripts" never fixed.
!bin/mhm-migrate-meta.php
# One-shot maintenance script for reverting prematurely auto-completed bookings
# (paired with the AutoComplete cron fix in 6b51cb0). Live-verified end-to-end.
!bin/cleanup-early-completed-bookings.php
# Quality-gate script: `composer check-guarded-refs` requires it at runtime
# and Task 3 wires it into CI, so it must ship in every clone.
!bin/assert-tests-ran.php
!bin/check-guarded-refs.php
# Quality-gate script: `composer check-uicore-version` requires it at runtime and
# CI invokes it, so it must ship in every clone. It locks the hand-written version
# literal in mhm-rentiva.php to the ui-core package actually installed; the literal
# cannot be read from the package because registration precedes any bootstrap.
!bin/check-uicore-version.php

# The React endpoint-map gate. Lives here rather than in the add-on because this
# repo CI is single-repo by design; the add-on runs the same file against its own
# map via MHM_API_* env overrides.
!bin/check-react-api-map.php
!bin/check-react-error-boundary.php
# Audit helpers for the defect classes WordPress.org's review kept surfacing.
# Deliberately REPORTS, not CI gates -- each prints what it cannot see before
# what it found, because a tool that under-reports while printing "0 found" is
# the same false confidence that let 500 phpcs suppressions read as clean.
# Tracked because the next submission (this plugin or another) has to be able to
# re-run them; see standards/wporg-submission-guidelines.md -> KANUN 0.
!bin/audit-object-capabilities.php
!bin/audit-control-classes.php
!bin/audit-phantom-callbacks.php
# Same family, added by the BookingForm round: it finds wp_send_json_* refusals
# with no return after them, which work only because wp_send_json_* ends the
# request through wp_die(). It reports rather than gates for a reason of its own,
# and the honest one is not "a variable function name could hide a call": it is
# that judging what follows a call needs a reachability model, and this one
# approximates. It already had to be taught that an explicit wp_die() terminates.
# An approximation that fails a build is a build failed by an approximation.
!bin/audit-json-fallthrough.php
# The exception to the "reports, not gates" rule above, and the reason it is an
# exception is worth stating. Those three make a JUDGEMENT (is this capability
# the right one?) and a judgement that under-reports must not fail a build.
# This one makes an INVENTORY claim -- "the set of user-account write sites in
# src/ is exactly this set" -- and a tokenizer cannot miss a literal call the
# way a call-graph walk can, so it is complete over the shape it looks for and
# safe to exit 1 on. It exists because WordPress.org's T9 review found a
# wp_update_user() in a service method that no handler reaches, which made it
# invisible to audit-object-capabilities.php (that one starts from registered
# handlers). Tracked with its input for the same reason lite-manifest-final.txt
# is: a gate whose data file is untracked is not a gate.
!bin/audit-user-account-writes.php
!bin/user-write-inventory.txt
# Quality-gate script: `composer crippleware` / `composer carve-gates` require
# it at runtime; must ship in every clone (carve-out Task 1).
!bin/check-crippleware.php
# Quality-gate script: `composer check-manifest` / `composer carve-gates` require
# it at runtime; it asserts src/ == bin/lite-manifest-final.txt in both
# directions, so it must ship in every clone (carve-out Task 5c).
!bin/check-manifest.php
# ...and its INPUT, which is the half that was missing. The manifest used to be
# read from carveout/, which this file excludes, so the gate above shipped to
# every clone with nothing to compare against: it exited 1 for a missing file
# rather than a real mismatch, and no CI job ran it. Tracking the script but not
# the list it needs is the same as not having the gate.
!bin/lite-manifest-final.txt
!bin/check-shipped-surface.php
!bin/shipped-surface-final.txt
# Quality-gate script: `composer check-unguarded-pro-refs` / `composer carve-gates`
# require it at runtime; it is the inverse of check-guarded-refs.php (proves every
# Pro reference sits behind a guard, incl. in templates/ which PHPStan never
# scans), so it must ship in every clone (carve-out Task 7).
!bin/check-unguarded-pro-refs.php
# Quality-gate script: `composer check-external-http` / `composer carve-gates`
# require it at runtime; it deny-lists third-party hosts (Lite must make no
# third-party HTTP calls), so it must ship in every clone (carve-out Task 8).
!bin/check-external-http.php
# CI needs a canonical WP test-suite installer (tests/bootstrap.php references
# it); Task 3 wires it into the phpunit CI job, so it must ship in every clone.
!bin/install-wp-tests.sh
# Quality-gate script: `composer check-no-pro-refs` / `composer carve-gates`
# require it at runtime; it is the WP.org compliance oracle asserting Lite
# ships zero edition/license/gating tokens, so it must ship in every clone
# (Task A12).
!bin/check-no-pro-refs.php
# Quality-gate script: `composer check-react-imports` requires it at runtime and
# the static-analysis CI job wires it in, so it must ship in every clone. It
# asserts every third-party module src-react/ imports is declared in
# package.json -- the gap that let chart.js build from an `extraneous`
# node_modules install for two months (fixed in b534cb53).
!bin/check-react-imports.php
# Quality-gate script: `php bin/check-shape-zero.php` requires it at runtime; it
# is Gate G-A (WP.org T7 remediation) -- zero visible NonceVerification.Missing /
# EscapeOutput / ValidatedSanitizedInput shapes under --ignore-annotations,
# with one narrow allowed residual (NonceVerification.Recommended on four
# named admin list-table display files, under a ceiling). The static-analysis
# CI job wires it in with continue-on-error while it is red; it must ship in
# every clone (WP.org T7 remediation, Task 1).
!bin/check-shape-zero.php
# Quality-gate script: `php bin/check-instrument-gaps.php` requires it at
# runtime; it is Gate G-B (WP.org T7 remediation, Task 2) -- five grep-based
# probes for shapes phpcs/WPCS is structurally blind to but WP.org's reviewer
# flagged anyway (filter_input UNSAFE_RAW/DEFAULT, CSS-context strip_tags,
# unkeyed array_map into update_option, third-party host strings, and the
# multiline compound-nonce-condition shape). Complementary to G-A, not a
# duplicate of it. Wired into CI with continue-on-error while it is red; must
# ship in every clone.
!bin/check-instrument-gaps.php
# Quality-gate script: `php bin/check-prefix-inventory.php` requires it at
# runtime; it is Gate G-C (WP.org T7 remediation, Task 3) -- six modes
# (bijection, post_type/taxonomy length limits, baseline-coverage, post-sweep
# no-old-names, options-call coverage, cron-hook coverage) that verify
# PrefixMigrationMap.php (the single source of truth Task 12's rename sweep
# and Task 13's DB migration both read) is complete before either of those
# later tasks may rely on it. Wired into CI with continue-on-error while
# mode 4 is red (no sweep has run yet); must ship in every clone.
!bin/check-prefix-inventory.php
# INPUT to the gate above and to Task 12/13: the raw prefix-name inventory
# extracted straight from source (bin/check-prefix-inventory.php's mode 3
# reads it). Tracking the gate but not the data it checks against would be
# the same gap check-manifest.php's missing lite-manifest-final.txt already
# taught this repo to avoid -- see that entry above.
!bin/prefix-inventory-baseline.txt
# Quality-gate script: `php bin/check-plugin-check-parity.php` requires it at
# runtime; it is Gate G-D (WP.org T7 remediation) -- runs WP.org's Plugin Check
# ITSELF (`wp plugin check --categories=plugin_repo`, in the Docker WP stack)
# over the surface .distignore actually ships, and counts ERRORS/WARNINGS
# separately. The acceptance bar is 0 errors AND every warning matched one to
# one by bin/gd-accepted-warnings.json (see that entry below);
# G-A/G-B/G-C above are narrower probes that sit under it. Measured baseline
# after the EscapeOutput fixes: 2 errors / 99 warnings. Must ship in every
# clone.
!bin/check-plugin-check-parity.php
# G-D's documented warning acceptance (owner decision 2026-08-08): the residual
# Plugin Check warnings (mandatory DDL + read-only GET reads), each worked and
# justified, keyed file|code with counts. The gate fails on any warning above
# an accepted count AND on any stale entry, so this file can only shrink.
# Tracking the gate but not the data it checks against would repeat the
# check-manifest gap documented above.
!bin/gd-accepted-warnings.json
# bin/plugin-check.ruleset.xml (a vendored copy of Plugin Check's ruleset) was
# deleted on 2026-08-02 and deliberately has no entry here. It was missing
# WordPress.Security.EscapeOutput and had the four PluginCheck.* sniff refs
# stripped, so the gate that ran it reported 1 error where the real tool
# reported 4 -- two of them EscapeOutput, the family the fifth WP.org review
# rejected this plugin over. The gate now shells out to the installed
# plugin-check plugin; there is no local ruleset copy to keep in sync, which is
# the point.
# Görev 12's rename tool. Not shipped (.distignore excludes bin/), but it is
# the executable definition of the 6.0.0 rename and G-C mode 4b requires it,
# so it must be tracked like the other gate scripts.
!bin/prefix-rename.php
# Görev 0 of the 2026-08-03 T8 remediation round: the before/after instrument
# for Görev 1's deletion of the core-table index subsystem. Counts CREATE/DROP
# INDEX call sites in source plus live-owned indexes in the database.
# Deliberately reports (declares its own blind spots on every run) rather than
# gates -- same "audit helper" shape as audit-object-capabilities.php and its
# neighbours above. Tracked so this round's later tasks, and any future round,
# can re-run it.
!bin/audit-index-surface.php
# Görev 5 of the 2026-08-03 T8 remediation round: the tag-context markup
# checker (F21). Its collector is require()d directly by
# tests/Tools/TemplateLiteralMarkupCheckerTest.php as the standing PHPUnit
# guard; its CLI mode also runs the same collector as a per-file sweep over
# the whole shipped JS surface (no python dependency, unlike
# bin/build-release.py --list-shipped, which the CLI mode's file walk was
# verified equivalent to at task time). Tracked so both the test and any
# future manual/CI sweep can run it.
!bin/check-template-literal-markup.php
# Gate G-E of the 2026-08-05 T9 round: ESLint's probable-bug rule set over the
# shipped JS surface, scope derived from bin/build-release.py --list-shipped
# (same oracle as Gate G-D). Exists because the previous round scoped its
# ESLint work to no-undef alone and three real defects survived into the
# submission candidate. Host-run: ESLint needs node, which the PHPUnit
# container does not have -- the same documented host-only shape as
# check-plugin-check-parity.php. Tracked so any future round can re-run it.
!bin/check-js-correctness.php
# G-E: finds admin-only core functions called from paths that never load
# wp-admin. It exists because /customers/bulk called wp_delete_user() -- which
# lives in wp-admin/includes/user.php -- and fataled on every real dispatch
# while PHPUnit, PHPCS, PHPStan and Plugin Check were all green over it. Must
# be tracked or the gate that catches that class ships in nobody's clone.
!bin/check-admin-only-functions.php
# Task 5 of the 2026-08-19 refund/deposit slice 2 round: the M-02 sweep's own
# inventory probe. Reports fixed-100 minor-unit conversions the sweep (Tasks
# 2-4) did not reach; declares its starting set and blind spots rather than
# gating. Tracked so the next round can re-run it. `bin/*` above ignores this
# directory itself, so the fixture directory needs its own negation before its
# file's negation -- a parent-directory exclusion cannot be undone from below.
!bin/audit-fixed-minor-scale.php
!bin/fixtures/
!bin/fixtures/fixed-minor-scale-fixture.txt
# Task 13 of the 2026-08-19 refund/deposit slice 3 round: reports every
# remaining mention of the two retired payment-amount meta keys
# (_mhmrentiva_payment_amount, _mhmrentiva_booking_payment_amount), the way
# audit-fixed-minor-scale.php above reports its own defect class. Declares its
# starting set (every git-tracked file) and blind spots (runtime-assembled
# keys, compiled JS, the Pro tree) rather than gating. Tracked so the next
# round -- or a re-check of this one -- can re-run it.
!bin/audit-retired-meta.php
# Task 2 of the 2026-08-21 refund/deposit slice 5 round: the single-writer
# gate for _mhmrentiva_refund_status. `composer check-refund-status-writers` /
# `composer carve-gates` require it at runtime; it is the CLI twin of
# tests/Gates/RefundStatusSingleWriterTest.php, so a developer or CI job
# without a PHPUnit environment still has the invariant enforced. Must ship
# in every clone or the gate that catches a bare update_post_meta() bypassing
# RefundStatus::transition() runs in nobody's clone but this one.
!bin/check-refund-status-writers.php
# Translation placeholder gate. `composer check-i18n-placeholders` and the CI
# step run it, and tests/Gates/I18nPlaceholderParityTest.php require()s it --
# so an untracked copy would fail the suite in every clean clone, exactly the
# way the missing bin/mhm-migrate-meta.php did. It catches the class msgfmt -c
# cannot see: a translation that changes a {{placeholder}} rather than the
# words around it. Seven Turkish e-mail subjects shipped {{booking.id}} where
# the source says {{booking.order_id}}.
!bin/check-i18n-placeholders.php
# Design-token definition gate. `composer check-token-definitions` runs it and
# tests/Gates/TokenDefinitionClassificationTest.php require()s it, so an
# untracked copy would fail the suite in every clean clone. It exists because
# three rounds of prose could not pin down what "shared token" means: measured
# 2026-08-27, `--mhm-primary` was declared 33 times behind five expressions and
# three fallback colours, so one name painted a different blue depending on
# which stylesheet's selector matched. The classification lives in this file
# and nowhere else -- the gate IS the specification.
!bin/check-token-definitions.php
# Style dependency gate, the other half of the token slice. `composer
# check-style-token-deps` runs it and tests/Gates/StyleTokenDependencyTest.php
# require()s it. Measured 2026-08-27: 28 registrations enqueue a token-reading
# stylesheet without reaching the canonical handle -- including the paid
# plugin enqueueing the free plugin's user-dashboard.css with array()
# (VendorLedger.php:36). Those pages stay coloured only because the copied
# declaration blocks are still there, so the copies cannot be deleted until
# this gate is green.
!bin/check-style-token-deps.php
# The dependency gate's baseline: the eleven call sites it cannot read
# statically, each inspected once and found sound. Locked as a SET of
# file:line, not a count -- a count stays eleven when one is fixed and a
# different one appears, and the new one would ride in behind it. The gate
# fails on any drift in either direction.
!bin/token-deps-unresolved.txt
tools/
